                <pb facs="0138" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg54"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. May to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the Russian minister for foreign affairs says reports of
                    proposed convention between Russia and China relating to Manchuria are wholly
                    untrue; that the Russian Government has no intention to exclude other countries
                    from advantages now enjoyed in Manchuria, or to confer monopolies upon Russians;
                    that nothing will be done to close open door or hamper American commerce; same
                    assurances given at Washington by Russian ambassador.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
